**Summary:**

The bug was a classic off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). This caused:
1. `test_basic` to fail - returned 'world' instead of 'hello'
2. `test_single` to error - IndexError when trying to access index 1 of a single-element list

The fix was simple: changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`, and now all tests pass.
